  "body": "## Summary\n\nThe ```swap``` and the ```multihop``` functions lack a deadline parameter, allowing transactions to execute at unfavourable prices after sitting in the mempool due to network congestion or low gas fees.\n\nUsers are forced to accept their minimum slippage thresholds even when market conditions have significantly deteriorated since transaction submission, resulting in up to slippage % value loss.\n\n## Vulnerability Details\n\nAMMs should provide their users with an option to limit the time of the execution of their pending actions, such as swaps or adding and removing liquidity.\n\nThe most common solution is to include a deadline timestamp as a parameter as it has been done correctly in this ```swapExactTokensForTokens``` function.  \n\n```solidity\nfunction swapExactTokensForTokens(\n    uint256 amountIn,\n    uint256 amountOutMin,\n    Route[] calldata routes,\n    address to,\n    uint256 deadline // <- Deadline protection\n) external ensure(deadline)\n```  \n```solidity\nmodifier ensure(uint256 deadline) {\n    require(block.timestamp <= deadline, 'Transaction too old');\n    _;\n}\n```  \nWithout a deadline parameter, users transactions can be executed at unexpected times when market conditions are unfavourable. \n\nThe affected function in ```Router.sol```: \n\n```solidity\nfunction swap(\n    PoolKey memory poolKey, \n    bool isToken1, \n    int128 amount, \n    SqrtRatio sqrtRatioLimit, \n    uint256 skipAhead\n    // <- Missing deadline parameter\n) external payable\n```  \nThe other affected functions in ```Router.sol``` are:\n\n- ```swap()``` (all overloads)\n- ```multihopSwap()```\n- ```multiMultihopSwap()```\n\n***Example Scenario:***\n1) Alice submits swap at 10:00 AM: 3000 USDC → 1 WETH (minimum 2990 USDC worth)\n2) Transaction has low gas priority, sits in mempool during network congestion\n3) At 3:00 PM, market crashes (-20%), her transaction finally executes\n4) Alice receives exactly her minimum (2990 USDC worth), but this is now only 0.83 WETH instead of 1 WETH\n5) With deadline protection: If Alice set deadline = 10:30 AM, transaction would revert at 10:31 AM, allowing her to resubmit with updated parameters reflecting current market conditions\n\n## Impact\n\n1) Forced Execution at Stale Prices: Users transactions can execute hours or days after submission when market conditions have drastically changed, forcing them to accept outdated slippage parameters\n2) Transactions sitting in mempool for extended periods become targets for MEV bots who can wait for optimal conditions to include the stale transaction for maximum extraction\n\n## Mitigation\nAdd deadline check to the ```swap()``` and ```multihop``` functions\n```solidity\nfunction swap(\n    PoolKey memory poolKey,\n    bool isToken1,\n    int128 amount,\n    SqrtRatio sqrtRatioLimit,\n    uint256 skipAhead,\n    int256 calculatedAmountThreshold,\n    uint256 deadline, // <- Added deadline\n    address recipient \n) public payable ensure(deadline) // <- modifier checking deadline\n```",
